---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import { PanelScreen } from '../components/Panel/PanelScreen'
---

<BaseLayout title="Panel — MorseForge" description="Usage summary." path="/panel/" private>
  <main class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-6 py-14">
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-4xl">Panel</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted">
      Counted from nginx&rsquo;s own access log by a job on the server. No analytics service, no
      database, nothing added to the page for visitors.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-10">
      <PanelScreen client:load />
    </div>

    <section class="mt-16 border-t border-line pt-10 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">
      <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink">
        What is actually stored
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-3">
        The summariser hashes each address with a salt that changes daily and counts the hash, then
        throws it away. No address, no user agent and no individual path is ever written to the
        summary — so the file this page reads could be published tomorrow without exposing anyone.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3">
        Visitors can turn the event counts off in{' '}
        <a href="/settings/" class="text-signal underline underline-offset-4">settings</a>, and they
        are never sent at all from a browser that asks not to be tracked. Both of those mean the
        numbers here are a floor, not a census.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3">
        This page is not linked from anywhere, is disallowed in robots.txt and carries a noindex.
        The password on it is the part that actually protects it.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
